summary:
  A member counts as there when some file of the package declares it, not
  the file the name leads to.

history:
  The names repeat across files: SyncEngine.qml, TimeshiftEngine.qml and
  four more have a root called `engine`, most engines have `app` and `cfg`,
  and a property such as `lag` exists on the sync engine and not on
  main.qml. `root.lag` written in the popup is `undefined`, and a check
  that asks "is it declared anywhere" calls it fine. What makes the check
  worth having is that it asks the one file the wiring points at.

target:
  tests/test_cross_file_members.py

find:
          if member in f.members or member in inherited:

replace:
          if any(member in g.members for g in self.files.values()) or member in inherited:

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cross_file_members.py::test_a_member_has_to_be_at_the_root_of_the_file_the_name_leads_to,
  whose `root.lag` and `app.lag` are declared, in the other file.
